# Initial implementation record

This is the initial baseline, not an optimization round. Optimization hypotheses
used: **0** (no group commit). No performance comparison or language claim is made.
All commands ran through the pinned Linux broker; source edits stayed local.

| Attempt/check | Observation | Action/result |
|---|---|---|
| Infrastructure/ABI reading | Arena creation succeeded for 0 and 16 MiB; 16 MiB + 1 returned null. Header exposes arena ownership and v1 layouts. | Validate aggregate batch size before admission; retain source buffer and arena throughout native calls. |
| First release build | Built successfully with pinned offline crates. | Retained versions/checksums and dynamic adapter/RocksDB linkage. |
| Public smoke | Passed. | Proceeded to independent protocol/storage/crash tests. |
| Initial seven integration tests and SHA vectors | All passed, including three live cancellation/crash/restart cycles. | Added coverage for full recovery backlog, slow clients, framing, cancellation fixtures and request-stream crashes. |
| Output-queue review | Frame-count-only bounding could retain multiple large status responses per client; best-effort events could fill all response slots. | Allow one response in flight until actually written; reserve a response slot and cap events separately. Connection leases cover both reader and writer lifetime. Correctness/resource-bound fix, not an optimization experiment. |
| Expanded 12-test suite, first run | Eleven passed; request-stream crash test got ConnectionRefusedError during restart. Service diagnostic logs were empty. | Test harness had treated socket pathname existence as readiness; Unix bind creates the path before listen. Added an actual connection/EOF readiness probe and close-on-connect-failure cleanup. No service change for this failure. |
| Expanded suite after readiness fix | All 12 passed, plus SHA vectors and public smoke. | Confirmed pending work was actually retained in crash snapshots; independently inspected all database invariants. |
| Strict Clippy, first run | Five style diagnostics: fixed-size chunks, divisibility spelling, nested conditional. No compile/type/ownership error in service build. | Adopted pinned Rust array chunks/is_multiple_of and collapsed the conditional, then rebuilt/retested. |
| Artifact identification | `file` utility was unavailable. | Used ELF header/readelf and dynamic symbol inspection; confirmed Linux AArch64, dynamic RocksDB/rosetta, /adapter runpath and v1-only import. |
| Final validation | Strict Clippy passed. SHA vectors, public smoke and all 12 integration tests passed; integration runtime 7.382 seconds. | Final executable rebuilt from final source; artifact hashes saved in tmp/final-artifacts.json. |

The full-backlog test creates a valid stopped-writer recovery fixture with 1,024
jobs and 64 MiB pending payload. It exercises real native workers and actual sync
WriteBatches, with no barriers or scheduler hooks. Crash tests use SIGKILL at
selected live points; they do not simulate torn writes or hardware power loss.

No storage/native arena allocation failure was injected. No native sanitizer,
Miri-through-FFI, whole-service TSan, exhaustive race proof, or evaluator pass is
claimed. Initial preparation material and exact cost beyond observed elapsed
implementation time are unknown. Attempts and raw broker outputs remain in the
queue and test artifact directories; no failed repetition was substituted into a
performance result. The initial submission freezes on return.
